From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 17:01:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep RDD in detect-reporting mode

When arming the radar detector, mt7996 only issues RDD_START and never
puts the RDD into continuous detect-reporting mode. The firmware then
reports a radar event once and stops reporting on the operating channel
until the RDD is re-armed, which only happens on a channel switch
(mt7996_set_channel -> mt7996_dfs_init_radar_detector).

In hostapd DFS detect mode (DFS_DETECT_MODE) the AP intentionally does
not switch channels after a radar event, so the RDD is never re-armed and
detection goes silent after the first hit.

mt7915 already issues RDD_DET_MODE unconditionally at the end of
mt7915_dfs_start_rdd(); mt7996 was missing the equivalent call. Add it so
the firmware keeps reporting radar on the operating channel.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -3066,7 +3066,7 @@ static void mt7996_dfs_stop_radar_detect
 
 static int mt7996_dfs_start_rdd(struct mt7996_dev *dev, int rdd_idx)
 {
-	int region;
+	int err, region;
 
 	switch (dev->mt76.region) {
 	case NL80211_DFS_ETSI:
@@ -3081,7 +3081,11 @@ static int mt7996_dfs_start_rdd(struct m
 		break;
 	}
 
-	return mt7996_mcu_rdd_cmd(dev, RDD_START, rdd_idx, region);
+	err = mt7996_mcu_rdd_cmd(dev, RDD_START, rdd_idx, region);
+	if (err < 0)
+		return err;
+
+	return mt7996_mcu_rdd_cmd(dev, RDD_DET_MODE, rdd_idx, 1);
 }
 
 static int mt7996_dfs_start_radar_detector(struct mt7996_phy *phy)
